WEBVTT


00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:54.753
<i>Spain, 1944</i>


00:00:55.956 --> 00:00:57.324
<i>The Civil War is over.</i>


00:00:57.324 --> 00:00:59.459
<i>Hidden in the mountains,</i>


00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.662
<i>armed men are still fighting
the new Fascist regime.</i>


00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:03.926
<i>Military posts are established
to exterminate the Resistance.</i>


00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.820
A long time ago,


00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.861
in the Underground Realm,
where there are no lies or pain,


00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:42.925
there lived a princess who dreamt
of the human world.


00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:50.137
She dreamt of blue skies,
soft breeze and sunshine.


00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.442
One day,


00:01:57.184 --> 00:02:00.813
eluding her keepers,
the princess escaped.


00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:08.718
Once outside...


00:02:09.196 --> 00:02:12.825
the bright sun blinded her
and erased her memory.


00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:18.966
She forgot who she was
and where she came from.


00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:25.674
Her body suffered cold, sickness and pain.
And eventually she died.


00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.243
However, her father, the king,


00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.575
always knew that the Princess' soul
would return,


00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.553
perhaps in another body,


00:02:35.222 --> 00:02:37.747
in another place, at another time.


00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:41.685
He would wait for her,
until he drew his last breath,


00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:45.327
until the world stopped turning.


00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.698
Why did you bring
so many books, Ofelia?


00:02:56.877 --> 00:02:59.471
We're going to the country,
the outdoors.


00:03:04.985 --> 00:03:06.646
Fairy tales?


00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:11.149
You're a bit too old to be filling your head
with such nonsense.


00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.127
Ask him to stop the car.


00:03:30.277 --> 00:03:33.110
Ofelia, wait.


00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.406
Your brother's not well.


00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.177
Madam, are you okay?


00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:47.987
Ofelia?


00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.291
Ofelia, Come here.


00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.727
- I saw a fairy.
- Just look at your shoes!


00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:01.956
Let's go.


00:05:03.103 --> 00:05:06.004
When we get to the mill,
come out to greet the Captain.


00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:08.070
I want you to call him Father.


00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:10.942
You have no idea
how good he's been to us.


00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:15.644
It's just a word, Ofelia...
just a word...


00:05:41.575 --> 00:05:43.304
They're coming, Captain.


00:05:44.311 --> 00:05:45.801
15 minutes late.


00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:04.923
Carmen.


00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.702
Welcome.


00:06:18.545 --> 00:06:20.945
That's not necessary.
I can walk perfectly well.


00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:23.882
Doctor Ferreiro prefers
that you don't exert yourself.


00:06:24.618 --> 00:06:25.448
No.


00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.489
Come.
Do it for me.


00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:36.753
Thank you.


00:06:38.665 --> 00:06:39.791
Ofelia, come out.


00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.894
Say hello to the Captain.


00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:47.997
Ofelia.


00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.344
It's the other hand, Ofelia.


00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:03.312
Mercedes!


00:07:04.591 --> 00:07:07.424
- Bring the luggage.
- Sir.


00:08:13.126 --> 00:08:14.684
It's a labyrinth.


00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:20.756
Just a pile of old rocks
that have always been here.


00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.059
Even before the mill.


00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.071
Better not to go in there.
You may get lost.


00:08:27.707 --> 00:08:28.901
Thank you.


00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:30.773
Have you read them all?


00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:32.209
Mercedes!


00:08:34.314 --> 00:08:35.303
The Captain is calling.


00:08:37.851 --> 00:08:38.977
Your father needs me.


00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:43.047
He's not my father.


00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.482
The Captain is not my father.


00:08:45.658 --> 00:08:48.991
My father was a tailor.
He died in the war.


00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:50.460
He's not my father.


00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:54.299
You've made that clear enough.
Shall we go?


00:08:55.135 --> 00:08:56.796
Have you seen my mother?


00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:58.862
- Isn't she beautiful!
- Yes.


00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:01.671
She's sick with baby.
Did you notice?


00:09:19.526 --> 00:09:21.323
The guerrillas are sticking
to the woods


00:09:21.628 --> 00:09:23.425
because it's hard
to track them up there.


00:09:24.631 --> 00:09:26.895
Those bastards know the terrain
better than any of us.


00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:28.727
We'll block all access
to the woods


00:09:30.103 --> 00:09:33.163
Food, medicine-
we'll store it all. Right here.


00:09:33.373 --> 00:09:36.240
We need to force them down,
make them come to us.


00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:38.305
We'll set up three
new command posts.


00:09:38.478 --> 00:09:42.073
Here, here and here.


00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:43.272
Mercedes.


00:09:44.551 --> 00:09:47.076
- Ask Dr. Ferreiro to come down.
- Yes, sir.


00:09:51.758 --> 00:09:53.885
This will help you sleep
through the night.


00:09:55.195 --> 00:09:57.686
Just two drops just before bed.


00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:02.026
Two drops only.


00:10:04.571 --> 00:10:05.401
Very good.


00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.570
All of it.
Good.


00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:15.536
Don't hesitate to call me
if you need anything. Day or night.


00:10:17.951 --> 00:10:20.181
You or your nurse.


00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:21.976
Good night.


00:10:23.189 --> 00:10:25.521
Close the door
and turn off the lights, sweetie.


00:10:37.971 --> 00:10:39.666
You have to help us.
Come up and see him.


00:10:39.906 --> 00:10:43.137
The wound is getting worse.
His leg isn't any better.


00:10:47.213 --> 00:10:49.078
This is all I could get.


00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:50.304
I'm sorry.


00:10:52.185 --> 00:10:54.210
Captain Vidal is waiting
for you in his office.


00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.713
Come here, Ofelia.


00:11:33.927 --> 00:11:37.158
Jesus, your feet.
They're frozen!


00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.164
Are you afraid?


00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:51.400
A little.


00:11:56.482 --> 00:11:57.608
What's that noise?


00:11:57.717 --> 00:12:00.811
Nothing, just the wind.


00:12:02.288 --> 00:12:05.485
Nights here are different
from city nights.


00:12:06.426 --> 00:12:09.452
There, you hear cars-tramway.


00:12:09.996 --> 00:12:11.861
Here the houses are old.


00:12:13.633 --> 00:12:14.622
They creak.


00:12:17.203 --> 00:12:18.568
As if they were speaking.


00:12:22.608 --> 00:12:25.042
Tomorrow, I'm going
to give you a surprise.


00:12:25.812 --> 00:12:27.404
- A surprise?
- Yes.


00:12:28.948 --> 00:12:33.385
- A book?
- No, something much better.


00:12:39.359 --> 00:12:41.327
Why did you have to get married?


00:12:45.565 --> 00:12:47.897
I was alone too long.


00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:51.629
I'm with you.
You weren't alone.


00:12:52.672 --> 00:12:54.162
You were never alone.


00:12:56.642 --> 00:13:00.373
When you're older, you'll understand.
It hasn't been easy for me either.


00:13:04.017 --> 00:13:05.951
Your brother's at it again-


00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:08.946
Tell him one of your stories.


00:13:09.489 --> 00:13:11.184
I'm sure that'll calm down.


00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:17.652
My brother, my brother...


00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:25.270
Many, many years ago,


00:13:25.638 --> 00:13:28.004
in a sad, faraway land,


00:13:28.107 --> 00:13:31.838
there was an enormous mountain
made of rough, black stone.


00:13:32.512 --> 00:13:34.173
At sunset,


00:13:34.847 --> 00:13:37.111
on top of that mountain,


00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:41.787
a magic rose blossomed every night
that made whoever plucked it immortal.


00:13:42.121 --> 00:13:45.557
But no one dared go near it


00:13:46.025 --> 00:13:49.188
because its thorns were full of poison.


00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:02.998
Men talked amongst themselves
about their fear of death,


00:14:03.076 --> 00:14:07.706
and pain, but never about the promise
of eternal life.


00:14:11.751 --> 00:14:19.624
And every day, the rose wilted
unable to bequeath its gift to anyone.


00:14:21.494 --> 00:14:26.090
Forgotten and lost at the top
of that cold, dark mountain,


00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:29.826
forever alone, until the end of time.


00:14:42.748 --> 00:14:43.680
Come in.


00:14:47.186 --> 00:14:48.983
- How is she?
- Very weak.


00:14:49.589 --> 00:14:50.954
She'll have as much rest
as as she needs.


00:14:51.157 --> 00:14:52.249
I'll sleep down here.


00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:58.920
- And my son?
- Pardon?


00:14:59.232 --> 00:15:01.063
Excuse us, Captain.


00:15:03.102 --> 00:15:05.161
My son, how is he?


00:15:05.938 --> 00:15:07.838
For the moment, there's no
reason to be alarmed.


00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:10.940
Very good.


00:15:12.879 --> 00:15:17.839
Captain, your wife should not have
traveled at such a late stage of pregnancy.


00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.786
- Is that your opinion?
- My professional opinion, yes, sir.


00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.394
A son should be born
wherever his father is.


00:15:30.897 --> 00:15:31.921
That's all.


00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:35.866
One more thing, Captain.


00:15:36.869 --> 00:15:38.894
What makes you so sure
the baby is a male?


00:15:41.207 --> 00:15:42.174
Don't fuck with me.


00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:46.638
At 8 o'clock we detected movement
in the northwestern sector.


00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:48.142
Gunfire.


00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.444
Sergeant Bayona searched the area
and captured a suspect.


00:15:55.321 --> 00:15:57.152
The other one's his son,
here from the town.


00:15:57.223 --> 00:15:59.623
Captain, my father
is an honest man.


00:15:59.759 --> 00:16:02.751
Let me judge that.
Take your hat off in front of me.


00:16:03.763 --> 00:16:06.425
We found this weapon on him.
It's been fired.


00:16:06.632 --> 00:16:08.327
My father was hunting
rabbits, Captain.


00:16:08.401 --> 00:16:09.959
Again, keep quiet.


00:16:20.646 --> 00:16:22.307
"No God, no country, no Master"?


00:16:22.782 --> 00:16:26.912
- Just like that-how do you like that?
- Red prpaganda, Captain.


00:16:27.053 --> 00:16:28.850
It's not propaganda, sir.


00:16:29.555 --> 00:16:31.853
It's an old almanac, Captain.


00:16:32.892 --> 00:16:34.553
We're just farmers.


00:16:36.162 --> 00:16:36.992
Go on.


00:16:38.231 --> 00:16:41.997
I went up into the woods, Captain.
To hunt for rabbits.


00:16:42.635 --> 00:16:44.762
For my daughters. They're sick.


00:16:46.372 --> 00:16:47.839
Rabbits, uh?


00:16:48.241 --> 00:16:52.041
Captain, if my father says so,
he was hunting rabbits.


00:17:03.422 --> 00:17:05.117
Leave him alone.


00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:11.325
You killed him,
You killed him!


00:17:11.831 --> 00:17:14.823
Murderer!
Son of a bitch!


00:17:44.597 --> 00:17:46.758
Maybe you'll learn to search
these assholes properly


00:17:47.033 --> 00:17:48.591
before you come bothering me.


00:17:48.868 --> 00:17:50.028
Yes, Captain.


00:18:10.289 --> 00:18:13.725
Mother.
Mother, wake up!


00:18:14.226 --> 00:18:17.491
Mother, there's something in the room.


00:18:58.904 --> 00:18:59.836
Hello.


00:19:00.706 --> 00:19:02.230
Did you follow me here?


00:19:03.008 --> 00:19:04.168
Are you a fairy?


00:19:06.645 --> 00:19:07.509
Look!


00:19:12.852 --> 00:19:14.342
This is a fairy.


00:19:42.148 --> 00:19:43.809
You want me to go with you?


00:19:45.418 --> 00:19:47.852
Outside? Where?


00:21:05.865 --> 00:21:07.526
Hello?


00:21:08.901 --> 00:21:10.425
Hello?


00:21:28.487 --> 00:21:30.580
Echo.


00:21:37.596 --> 00:21:39.621
Echo.


00:21:42.501 --> 00:21:44.594
Hello?


00:21:47.439 --> 00:21:48.963
Hello?


00:21:51.577 --> 00:21:52.874
It's you.


00:21:58.017 --> 00:22:01.350
It's you.
You've returned.


00:22:01.453 --> 00:22:03.478
Don't be frightened,
I beg you.


00:22:04.823 --> 00:22:06.757
Look, look.


00:22:15.034 --> 00:22:17.662
My name is Ofelia.
Who are you?


00:22:17.803 --> 00:22:18.963
Me?


00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:24.008
I've had so many names...


00:22:24.209 --> 00:22:32.207
Old names that only the wind
and the trees can pronounce.


00:22:32.384 --> 00:22:39.222
I am the mountain,
the forest and the earth.


00:22:40.025 --> 00:22:41.322
I am...


00:22:44.797 --> 00:22:47.595
I am a faun.


00:22:48.367 --> 00:22:52.394
Your most humble servant,
Your Highness.


00:22:52.538 --> 00:22:56.167
- No, I'm...
- You're Princess Moanna,


00:22:56.275 --> 00:23:01.941
daughter of the king
of the underworld.


00:23:02.014 --> 00:23:03.743
My father was a tailor.


00:23:03.849 --> 00:23:05.976
You are not born of man.


00:23:07.019 --> 00:23:09.453
It was the moon that bore you.


00:23:09.622 --> 00:23:11.920
Look on your left shoulder


00:23:12.091 --> 00:23:15.060
and you will find a mark
that proves it.


00:23:15.494 --> 00:23:25.460
Your real father had us open portals
all over the world to allow your return.


00:23:25.938 --> 00:23:27.599
This is...


00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.834
This is the last of them.


00:23:31.477 --> 00:23:40.078
But we have to make sure
that your essence is intact,


00:23:40.586 --> 00:23:44.716
that you have not become a mortal.


00:23:48.293 --> 00:23:53.925
You must complete three tasks
before the moon is full.


00:23:56.869 --> 00:24:02.899
This is The Book of Crossroads.


00:24:03.609 --> 00:24:06.737
Open it, when you are alone


00:24:06.879 --> 00:24:09.780
and it will show you your future,


00:24:09.882 --> 00:24:14.216
show you what must be done.


00:24:22.594 --> 00:24:24.152
But there's nothing in here.


00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:24.681
Mercedes, prepare these rabbits
for dinner tonight.


00:25:25.691 --> 00:25:27.716
They are too young.


00:25:28.227 --> 00:25:31.287
- Well, maybe they'll do for a stew.
- Yes, sir.


00:25:33.766 --> 00:25:36.758
This coffee was burnt.
Taste it yourself.


00:25:45.210 --> 00:25:48.043
You should keep an eye on it.


00:25:49.848 --> 00:25:51.281
As you wish, sir.


00:25:57.823 --> 00:25:58.812
Cook these.


00:26:00.592 --> 00:26:03.060
- He didn't like the coffee.
- He's nothing but a fussy dandy.


00:26:03.195 --> 00:26:04.096
A fussy dandy!


00:26:04.096 --> 00:26:06.398
We're going to need some beef
and one more chicken.


00:26:06.398 --> 00:26:10.232
- Where are we supposed to find that?
- The doctor's wife, the mayor's too.


00:26:10.302 --> 00:26:13.294
Well, they eat more
than a couple of pigs.


00:26:14.406 --> 00:26:17.967
- And they don't shut up.
- Not even underwater.


00:26:32.925 --> 00:26:34.950
I'll be back in a moment,
Mercedes.


00:26:40.065 --> 00:26:41.327
Ofelia.


00:26:43.902 --> 00:26:46.632
Your father is giving
a dinner party tonight.


00:26:47.039 --> 00:26:49.872
Look what I've made for you.


00:26:51.310 --> 00:26:52.504
Do you like it?


00:26:54.313 --> 00:26:57.305
What I wouldn't have given
to have such a dress...


00:26:57.449 --> 00:26:59.883
as fine as this when I was your age!


00:27:00.052 --> 00:27:01.178
And look at the shoes!


00:27:02.554 --> 00:27:05.250
- Do you like them?
- Yes, very pretty.


00:27:06.892 --> 00:27:08.553
Go on, now.
Take your bath.


00:28:12.925 --> 00:28:13.914
Ofelia?


00:28:15.694 --> 00:28:16.558
Ofelia?


00:28:17.996 --> 00:28:21.454
Hurry up.
I want to see the dress on you.


00:28:21.733 --> 00:28:24.293
I want you to be beautiful
for the Captain.


00:28:27.139 --> 00:28:28.902
You'll look like a princess.


00:28:33.312 --> 00:28:34.711
A princess?


00:28:41.053 --> 00:28:42.782
Make sure those chickens
are cleaned properly.


00:28:42.888 --> 00:28:45.356
And don't forget the beans.


00:28:48.593 --> 00:28:52.962
- You look marvelous, my girl, just beautiful.
- What a gorgeous dress!


00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:57.891
Get back to work,
stop wasting time.


00:29:00.706 --> 00:29:02.173
Do you want some milk with honey?


00:29:07.713 --> 00:29:11.672
Move back, we can't have you getting
milk on your dress, with you looking so pretty.


00:29:14.052 --> 00:29:17.988
Mercedes.
Do you believe in fairies?


00:29:19.124 --> 00:29:20.022
No.


00:29:20.826 --> 00:29:22.191
But when I was a little girl,
I did.


00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:24.854
I believed in a lot of things
I don't believe any more.


00:29:27.265 --> 00:29:28.994
Last night,
a fairy visited me.


00:29:30.002 --> 00:29:31.060
Really?


00:29:32.304 --> 00:29:35.440
And it wasn't alone,
there were lots of them,


00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:37.135
- And a faun, too.
- A faun?


00:29:37.409 --> 00:29:41.368
He was very old, very tall
and smelled like earth.


00:29:42.414 --> 00:29:45.440
My mother warned me
to be wary of fauns.


00:29:45.684 --> 00:29:46.742
Mercedes!


00:29:48.687 --> 00:29:49.654
Come with me.


00:30:00.332 --> 00:30:02.129
Captain,
everything is here.


00:30:02.367 --> 00:30:05.063
Flour, salt, oil, medicine,


00:30:05.237 --> 00:30:08.365
olives, bacon.


00:30:09.474 --> 00:30:11.339
This-this is real tobacco.


00:30:12.310 --> 00:30:13.709
And the ration cards.


00:30:14.079 --> 00:30:16.411
- I need you to check the inventory.
- Very well.


00:30:19.885 --> 00:30:20.909
Mercedes.


00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:23.815
- The key.
- Yes, sir.


00:30:31.163 --> 00:30:33.097
- Is this the only copy?
- The only one.


00:30:33.198 --> 00:30:34.995
From now on, I'll carry it.


00:30:35.934 --> 00:30:36.866
Captain.


00:30:42.641 --> 00:30:44.233
Captain,
perhaps it's nothing.


00:30:52.651 --> 00:30:53.640
It's them.


00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:09.391
"Once upon a time,
when the forest was young,


00:31:09.968 --> 00:31:15.600
they were home to creatures
who were full of magic and wonder."


00:31:22.414 --> 00:31:24.746
"They protected one another,


00:31:25.050 --> 00:31:28.213
and slept in the shade
of a colossal fig tree


00:31:28.653 --> 00:31:31.087
that grew on a hill, near the mill."


00:31:33.625 --> 00:31:35.388
"But now, the tree is dying.


00:31:35.727 --> 00:31:39.390
Its branches are dry,
its trunk old and twisted.


00:31:40.198 --> 00:31:43.429
A monstrous toad
has settled in its roots


00:31:43.702 --> 00:31:45.169
and won't let the tree thrive.


00:31:46.471 --> 00:31:49.668
You must put the three magic
stones in the toad's mouth


00:31:50.342 --> 00:31:53.800
and retrieve the golden key
from inside his belly.


00:31:54.412 --> 00:31:57.575
Only then will the fig tree
flourish again."


00:33:24.102 --> 00:33:25.899
They were here
less than twenty minutes ago.


00:33:26.705 --> 00:33:28.536
They left in a hurry.


00:33:35.680 --> 00:33:37.580
A dozen men, at most.


00:33:56.501 --> 00:33:57.866
Antibiotics.


00:33:58.837 --> 00:34:02.000
Shit, they forgot this lottery ticket.


00:34:04.342 --> 00:34:05.536
They're here.


00:34:08.513 --> 00:34:10.879
Those sons of bitches are here.


00:34:11.750 --> 00:34:13.877
And they're watching us.


00:34:23.828 --> 00:34:25.523
Hey!


00:34:26.865 --> 00:34:29.356
You left this behind!


00:34:30.101 --> 00:34:32.092
And your lottery ticket!


00:34:32.637 --> 00:34:34.730
Why don't you come back
and get it?


00:34:35.473 --> 00:34:37.941
Who knows?
This could be your lucky day!


00:35:49.080 --> 00:35:52.641
Hello.
I'm Princess Moanna,


00:35:53.017 --> 00:35:54.484
and I'm not afraid of you.


00:35:57.956 --> 00:36:01.187
Aren't you ashamed
living down here,


00:36:01.393 --> 00:36:03.418
eating all these bugs...


00:36:04.195 --> 00:36:07.130
and growing fat
while the tree dies?


00:38:50.028 --> 00:38:52.053
Have you looked in her room?
And the pantry?


00:38:52.196 --> 00:38:53.458
Yes, ma'am.


00:38:57.068 --> 00:38:58.660
Have you checked the garden?


00:38:59.003 --> 00:39:00.800
- And the barn?
- Yes, ma'am.


00:39:01.639 --> 00:39:03.231
Where is that girl?


00:39:03.308 --> 00:39:04.605
This way, please.


00:39:05.643 --> 00:39:08.635
Let me to introduce you
to my wife, Carmen.


00:39:10.515 --> 00:39:12.380
- Charmed.
- A pleasure to meet you.


00:39:12.984 --> 00:39:16.283
From now on,
one ration card per family.


00:39:17.055 --> 00:39:18.022
Take a look.


00:39:18.156 --> 00:39:20.351
- One?
- Only one.


00:39:21.125 --> 00:39:22.922
Captain, I'm not sure
it'll be enough.


00:39:22.994 --> 00:39:24.325
If people are careful,
it should be plenty.


00:39:24.395 --> 00:39:27.592
We can't allow anyone to send food
to the guerillas in the mountains.


00:39:27.732 --> 00:39:31.600
They're losing ground,
and one of them is wounded.


00:39:32.470 --> 00:39:35.206
Excuse me, Captain,
how can you be so sure?


00:39:35.206 --> 00:39:37.936
We almost got them.
We found this.


00:39:38.743 --> 00:39:39.971
Antibiotics.


00:39:41.212 --> 00:39:43.578
God has already
saved their souls.


00:39:43.848 --> 00:39:46.476
What happens to their bodies
hardly matter to Him.


00:39:46.651 --> 00:39:49.142
We'll help however we can, Captain.


00:39:49.253 --> 00:39:51.414
We know you're not here by choice.


00:39:55.793 --> 00:39:56.851
You're wrong about that.


00:39:58.062 --> 00:40:01.930
I choose to be here because I want
my son to be born in a new, clean Spain.


00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:05.994
Because these people
hold the mistaken belief


00:40:06.270 --> 00:40:07.828
that we're all equal.


00:40:08.439 --> 00:40:09.906
But there's a big difference:


00:40:10.508 --> 00:40:13.033
The war is over and we won.


00:40:13.645 --> 00:40:16.580
And if we need to kill every one
of these vermin to settle it,


00:40:17.582 --> 00:40:19.743
then we'll kill them all,
and that's that.


00:40:20.985 --> 00:40:22.509
We're all here by choice.


00:40:23.521 --> 00:40:25.716
By choice!


00:40:28.626 --> 00:40:31.424
Put the coffee on.
I'm going for more wood.


00:40:31.562 --> 00:40:33.553
We'll take care of it.


00:41:00.558 --> 00:41:01.684
Ofelia?


00:41:13.705 --> 00:41:16.572
So, how did you
and the Captain meet?


00:41:19.010 --> 00:41:21.808
Ofelia's father used to make
the Captain's uniforms.


00:41:21.946 --> 00:41:22.913
Oh, I see...


00:41:23.448 --> 00:41:27.646
And after he died,
I went to work at the shop.


00:41:27.785 --> 00:41:29.980
A little more than a year ago,


00:41:30.888 --> 00:41:34.688
the Captain and I met again.


00:41:34.859 --> 00:41:36.349
Curious, isn't it!


00:41:36.627 --> 00:41:39.596
I mean, finding each other again?


00:41:41.132 --> 00:41:43.794
Oh, yes,
very, very curious.


00:41:44.068 --> 00:41:47.765
Please, forgive my wife.
She hasn't been exposed to the world.


00:41:48.272 --> 00:41:50.502
She thinks these silly stories
are interesting to others.


00:41:51.676 --> 00:41:53.200
We understand.


00:41:55.613 --> 00:41:57.774
Excuse me, madam
Ofelia is here.


00:41:58.516 --> 00:41:59.915
Excuse me.


00:42:10.862 --> 00:42:13.057
Have I told you that I was acquainted
with your father, Captain?


00:42:14.232 --> 00:42:15.699
No.
I had no idea.


00:42:18.436 --> 00:42:19.926
In Morocco.


00:42:20.338 --> 00:42:23.307
I knew him only briefly,
but he left a great impression.


00:42:23.374 --> 00:42:24.568
An excellent soldier.


00:42:25.042 --> 00:42:29.342
The men in his battalion said that
when General Vidal died on the battlefield,


00:42:30.148 --> 00:42:31.809
he smashed his watch on a rock


00:42:32.016 --> 00:42:34.507
so that his son would know
the exact hour and minute of his death.


00:42:35.620 --> 00:42:37.952
So he would know
how a brave man dies.


00:42:41.025 --> 00:42:43.550
Nonsense.
He didn't own a watch.


00:42:45.163 --> 00:42:48.360
What you've done hurts me.


00:42:49.901 --> 00:42:52.495
After your bath,
you'll go to bed without supper.


00:42:54.505 --> 00:42:55.597
Are you listening?


00:42:59.076 --> 00:43:01.840
Sometimes I think
you'll never learn to behave.


00:43:02.713 --> 00:43:04.704
You've disappointed me, Ofelia.


00:43:06.784 --> 00:43:08.183
And your father, too.


00:43:09.654 --> 00:43:10.916
You mean the Captain?


00:43:12.056 --> 00:43:13.353
Him more than me.


00:43:28.806 --> 00:43:30.239
I've got the key.


00:43:33.978 --> 00:43:35.605
Take me to the Labyrinth.


00:44:28.866 --> 00:44:29.855
Hello.


00:44:31.669 --> 00:44:33.466
I got the key out.


00:44:34.538 --> 00:44:39.407
That's me,
and the girl is you.


00:44:39.744 --> 00:44:40.938
And the baby?


00:44:42.313 --> 00:44:44.543
So... you retrieved the key.


00:44:47.318 --> 00:44:48.580
I'm glad.


00:44:57.228 --> 00:45:01.528
She believed in you
from the very beginning.


00:45:01.899 --> 00:45:04.595
She's so glad you succeeded.


00:45:10.641 --> 00:45:12.040
Keep the key.


00:45:12.476 --> 00:45:15.639
You'll be needing it very soon.


00:45:15.813 --> 00:45:20.716
And this too?
A piece of chalk.


00:45:22.153 --> 00:45:25.423
Two tasks remain


00:45:25.423 --> 00:45:30.258
and the moon is almost full.


00:45:30.361 --> 00:45:32.158
Be patient.


00:45:32.430 --> 00:45:41.134
We'll soon stroll through
the seven circular gardens of your palace.


00:45:41.238 --> 00:45:43.763
How do I know
that what you say is true?


00:45:44.075 --> 00:45:50.014
Why would a poor little faun
like me lie to you?


00:46:12.136 --> 00:46:13.330
Proceed.


00:46:14.372 --> 00:46:16.806
Have your cards
ready for inspection.


00:46:17.041 --> 00:46:19.601
Let's go.
Your name?


00:46:23.347 --> 00:46:24.837
Your names, first and last.


00:46:25.316 --> 00:46:29.480
Narciso Pena Soriano,
at your service.


00:46:32.990 --> 00:46:35.220
This is our daily bread
in Franco's Spain,


00:46:35.459 --> 00:46:39.555
kept safe in this mill!
The Reds lie...


00:46:39.930 --> 00:46:41.591
because in a united Spain,


00:46:41.766 --> 00:46:45.463
there's not a single home
without fire or bread.


00:46:59.683 --> 00:47:03.244
Come on, show me
what happens now?


00:47:03.754 --> 00:47:04.778
Show me.


00:47:42.827 --> 00:47:44.419
Ofelia, help me...


00:47:50.267 --> 00:47:52.132
Captain! Captain!


00:47:54.705 --> 00:47:56.263
Come quickly.


00:47:56.807 --> 00:47:58.104
...because in a united Spain,


00:47:58.209 --> 00:48:02.077
there's not a single home
without fire or bread.


00:48:02.546 --> 00:48:04.878
This is our daily bread
in Franco's Spain...


00:48:07.785 --> 00:48:10.754
Your wife needs
uninterrupted rest.


00:48:12.623 --> 00:48:15.524
She'll have to be sedated
most of the time.


00:48:17.761 --> 00:48:20.093
The girl should sleep
somewhere else.


00:48:21.866 --> 00:48:23.925
I'll stay here until the birth.


00:48:24.401 --> 00:48:25.368
Make her well.


00:48:26.704 --> 00:48:28.729
I don't care what it costs
or what you need.


00:48:33.444 --> 00:48:34.138
Make her well.


00:48:55.466 --> 00:48:56.933
Don't worry.


00:48:58.102 --> 00:49:00.593
Your mother will get better soon,
you'll see.


00:49:03.974 --> 00:49:05.601
Having a baby is complicated.


00:49:06.410 --> 00:49:09.573
Then I'll never have one.


00:49:22.126 --> 00:49:24.959
You're helping the men
in the woods, aren't you?


00:49:36.607 --> 00:49:37.938
Have you told anyone?


00:49:39.510 --> 00:49:40.636
No, I haven't.


00:49:42.846 --> 00:49:44.939
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you.


00:49:55.859 --> 00:49:57.121
Nor I to you.


00:49:58.662 --> 00:50:00.789
Do you know a lullaby?


00:50:02.766 --> 00:50:03.994
Only one...


00:50:05.135 --> 00:50:07.160
but I don't remember the words.


00:50:07.471 --> 00:50:11.066
I don't care.
I still want to hear it.


00:51:04.428 --> 00:51:07.192
Don't be afraid.
It's only me.


00:51:16.140 --> 00:51:18.108
- Are you ready?
- Yes.


00:51:19.276 --> 00:51:20.402
Then let's go.


00:51:25.416 --> 00:51:26.883
This is sheer madness.


00:51:27.251 --> 00:51:29.685
When that man finds out about us,
he'll kill us all.


00:51:30.187 --> 00:51:33.315
- Have you thought about that?
- Are you so afraid of him, Doctor?


00:51:33.724 --> 00:51:35.692
It's not fear...


00:51:36.293 --> 00:51:37.658
at least not for myself.


00:51:49.440 --> 00:51:50.839
Pedro!


00:51:51.141 --> 00:51:53.575
Pedro, My brother!


00:52:10.227 --> 00:52:12.388
You didn't carry out the task.


00:52:12.529 --> 00:52:15.828
No, my mother is sick.


00:52:17.368 --> 00:52:19.962
That's no excuse
for negligence.


00:52:20.237 --> 00:52:25.106
Look...
this is a mandrake root.


00:52:25.209 --> 00:52:29.077
A plant that dreamt
of being human.


00:52:30.013 --> 00:52:34.677
Put it under your mother's bed


00:52:35.052 --> 00:52:38.283
in a bowl of fresh milk.


00:52:38.889 --> 00:52:43.849
Each morning,
give it two drops of blood.


00:52:44.294 --> 00:52:48.355
Now, we have no time
to waste.


00:52:48.665 --> 00:52:51.429
The full moon will be upon us.


00:52:53.804 --> 00:52:56.272
Take my pets
to guide you through.


00:52:56.874 --> 00:53:02.471
You're going to a very dangerous
place, so be careful.


00:53:02.679 --> 00:53:05.443
The thing that slumbers there,


00:53:06.350 --> 00:53:08.875
it is not human.


00:53:12.723 --> 00:53:16.989
You will see
a sumptuous feast,


00:53:17.094 --> 00:53:19.892
but don't eat
or drink anything.


00:53:20.097 --> 00:53:24.830
Absolutely nothing.


00:53:26.503 --> 00:53:30.030
Your life depends on it.


00:53:50.694 --> 00:53:55.654
I've brought some Orujo,
tobacco, cheese.


00:53:56.366 --> 00:53:58.732
Mail for Trigo and Piloto.


00:54:00.804 --> 00:54:02.772
Let's see how that leg's doing,
Frenchie.


00:54:03.340 --> 00:54:06.776
How do you think it's doing?
It's fucked up.


00:54:07.244 --> 00:54:08.836
Let's see.


00:54:11.915 --> 00:54:15.180
...N- North American,


00:54:16.553 --> 00:54:19.215
British and Canadian troops


00:54:19.323 --> 00:54:22.850
disembarked on a small beach
in the North of F-F.


00:54:23.694 --> 00:54:26.390
- "France", idiot.
- F-f-f-rance.


00:54:26.797 --> 00:54:29.288
More than 150,000 soldiers
give us hope...


00:54:29.533 --> 00:54:34.334
under the command
of General Dwight D. Eisenhower...


00:54:34.538 --> 00:54:37.507
Is it really bad, doctor?


00:54:38.542 --> 00:54:40.169
Look, Frenchie.


00:54:41.445 --> 00:54:43.003
There's no way to save it.


00:54:54.892 --> 00:54:58.191
I'll try to make it
in as few cuts as possible.


00:55:05.969 --> 00:55:09.370
Wait a second, doctor,
just a second.


00:55:44.474 --> 00:55:50.640
"Use the chalk to trace a door
anywhere in your room."


00:55:55.819 --> 00:55:59.778
"Once the door's open,
start the hourglass."


00:56:02.092 --> 00:56:04.219
"Let the fairies guide you."


00:56:09.600 --> 00:56:12.933
"Don't eat or drink anything,
during your stay,


00:56:13.286 --> 00:56:17.848
And come back
before the last grain of sand falls."


00:58:26.819 --> 00:58:27.843
No...


00:58:30.690 --> 00:58:31.884
This other one.


01:01:07.780 --> 01:01:09.407
No! No!


01:02:25.224 --> 01:02:27.124
We'll soon have reinforcements
from Jaca.


01:02:27.560 --> 01:02:31.462
Fifty men or more.
Then we'll go head to head with Vidal.


01:02:32.498 --> 01:02:34.989
And then what?


01:02:35.701 --> 01:02:39.398
You kill him, they'll send another
just like him. And another...


01:02:39.972 --> 01:02:43.203
You're screwed, no guns,
no safe shelter...


01:02:43.309 --> 01:02:47.541
You need food, medicine.
You must take care of Mercedes.


01:02:47.780 --> 01:02:49.509
If you really love her,
you'd cross the border with her.


01:02:49.582 --> 01:02:52.016
- This is a lost cause.
- I'm staying here, doctor.


01:02:52.351 --> 01:02:53.318
There's no choice.


01:03:05.731 --> 01:03:06.891
You have to leave.


01:03:08.667 --> 01:03:11.602
Here's the key,
but you can't go down there now.


01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:14.101
It's exactly what he expects.


01:03:17.276 --> 01:03:18.243
Leave it to me.


01:03:22.314 --> 01:03:23.440
I'm a coward.


01:03:24.550 --> 01:03:27.075
No, you're not.


01:03:28.254 --> 01:03:29.482
Yes, I am.


01:03:30.122 --> 01:03:34.559
A coward... for living
next to that son of a bitch,


01:03:35.861 --> 01:03:38.659
doing his laundry, making his bed,
feeding him.


01:03:42.368 --> 01:03:44.859
What if the doctor's right
and we can't win?


01:03:49.175 --> 01:03:51.405
At least we'll make things
harder for that bastard.


01:05:46.292 --> 01:05:47.259
Captain Vidal...


01:05:49.361 --> 01:05:51.886
Her temperature's down.
I don't know how, but it is.


01:05:52.698 --> 01:05:53.630
But she still has a fever?


01:05:54.266 --> 01:05:57.167
Yes, but it's a good sign.
Her body is responding.


01:05:58.971 --> 01:05:59.938
Listen to me.


01:06:00.606 --> 01:06:03.632
If you have to choose,
save the baby.


01:06:03.809 --> 01:06:06.334
That boy will bear my name
and my father's name.


01:06:06.478 --> 01:06:07.467
Save him.


01:06:43.482 --> 01:06:44.449
Brother...


01:06:46.452 --> 01:06:47.384
Little brother...


01:06:49.621 --> 01:06:51.145
If you can hear me,


01:06:52.257 --> 01:06:54.418
things out here aren't too good.


01:06:56.295 --> 01:06:58.286
But soon you'll have to come out.


01:06:59.565 --> 01:07:01.192
You've made Mama very sick.


01:07:03.402 --> 01:07:07.031
I want to ask you one favor
for when you come out,


01:07:08.173 --> 01:07:09.299
just one:


01:07:10.642 --> 01:07:12.303
Don't hurt her.


01:07:13.512 --> 01:07:16.743
You'll meet her,
she's very pretty,


01:07:17.583 --> 01:07:19.847
even though sometimes she's sad
for days at a time.


01:07:20.953 --> 01:07:22.818
You'll see, when she smiles,


01:07:24.423 --> 01:07:25.913
you'll love her.


01:07:28.293 --> 01:07:31.592
Listen, if you do what I say,


01:07:31.897 --> 01:07:33.455
I'll make you a promise,


01:07:34.400 --> 01:07:38.029
I'll take you to my kingdom,
and I'll make you a prince.


01:07:39.037 --> 01:07:42.200
I promise you, a prince.


01:08:08.867 --> 01:08:11.392
I sounded the whistle,
but they wouldn't move.


01:08:11.603 --> 01:08:14.003
I tried to stop, but it was too late.


01:08:14.072 --> 01:08:16.506
The fireman and I
jumped outjust in time,


01:08:16.742 --> 01:08:18.141
but look at the mess they made.


01:08:21.313 --> 01:08:23.042
What did they steal
from the freight cars?


01:08:23.549 --> 01:08:25.346
They didn't open a single one.


01:08:25.617 --> 01:08:27.050
What the hell are you talking about?


01:08:27.186 --> 01:08:29.484
This whole mess...
They didn't open any of the cars.


01:08:29.688 --> 01:08:33.988
- They didn't take anything.
- Nothing? Are you sure?


01:08:34.359 --> 01:08:38.227
God only knows what they wanted,
other than to waste our time.


01:08:55.080 --> 01:08:56.843
They came out of nowhere, Captain.


01:09:00.185 --> 01:09:03.348
They have grenades,
they went up hill.


01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:10.858
Captain, we've surrounded
a small unit that fell behind.


01:09:11.096 --> 01:09:12.688
They took cover up on the hill.


01:09:47.766 --> 01:09:52.260
Go ahead, Serrano, don't be afraid,
this is the only decent way to die.


01:10:35.981 --> 01:10:37.175
Serrano!


01:10:54.399 --> 01:10:57.425
Let me see.


01:11:02.174 --> 01:11:03.266
Can you talk?


01:11:07.679 --> 01:11:08.646
Damn it!


01:11:27.232 --> 01:11:29.826
These are useless! They can't talk.


01:11:39.144 --> 01:11:41.806
Captain,
this one's still alive.


01:11:45.884 --> 01:11:47.249
Shot in the leg.


01:11:53.191 --> 01:11:54.556
- What's happened?
- They caught one.


01:11:54.660 --> 01:11:57.026
They took one of them alive.
And they're taking him to the storeroom.


01:12:02.234 --> 01:12:03.360
Mercedes!


01:12:04.202 --> 01:12:06.432
Pedro... Pedro...


01:12:23.889 --> 01:12:24.856
Mercedes?


01:12:25.791 --> 01:12:28.783
- I need to get into the storeroom.
- Not now.


01:12:29.294 --> 01:12:30.625
Move away!


01:12:57.723 --> 01:12:59.953
That's plenty, dear.


01:13:03.528 --> 01:13:05.018
Should I take this up?


01:13:24.883 --> 01:13:27.351
Here, half the dose.


01:13:27.853 --> 01:13:29.650
I don't think I need it.


01:13:29.955 --> 01:13:32.947
I feel better, much better.


01:13:33.225 --> 01:13:35.625
I don't understand.
But I'm glad.


01:13:38.964 --> 01:13:39.555
Mother...


01:13:54.312 --> 01:13:57.076
Damn, this cigarette is good!


01:13:57.849 --> 01:14:01.250
Real tobacco hard to find.


01:14:02.888 --> 01:14:05.288
G-G-Go to hell.


01:14:07.959 --> 01:14:11.952
Damn, Garces. We catch one
and he turns out to be a stutterer.


01:14:12.230 --> 01:14:14.357
We'll be here all night.


01:14:14.566 --> 01:14:16.534
As long as he talks.


01:14:22.407 --> 01:14:24.238
Garces is right.


01:14:25.076 --> 01:14:27.374
You'd do better
to tell us everything.


01:14:28.079 --> 01:14:31.446
But to make sure it happens,
I brought along a few tools.


01:14:33.785 --> 01:14:35.980
Just things you pick up
along the way.


01:14:36.188 --> 01:14:38.622
At first, I won't be able to trust you,


01:14:39.191 --> 01:14:42.649
but after I use this,
you'll own up to a few things.


01:14:44.696 --> 01:14:46.163
When we get to these,


01:14:47.199 --> 01:14:50.862
we'll have developed...
how can I put this-?


01:14:51.269 --> 01:14:53.863
A closer bond,
much like brothers.


01:14:55.307 --> 01:14:56.831
You'll see.


01:14:58.844 --> 01:15:00.505
And when we get to this one,


01:15:01.880 --> 01:15:04.314
I'll believe anything you tell me.


01:15:16.628 --> 01:15:17.925
I'll make you a deal.


01:15:17.996 --> 01:15:21.523
If you can count to three
without st-t-tuttering,


01:15:21.867 --> 01:15:23.061
you can go.


01:15:25.237 --> 01:15:28.172
Don't look at him, look at me.


01:15:28.440 --> 01:15:30.203
Above me, there's no one.


01:15:30.742 --> 01:15:32.642
- Garces!
- Yes, Captain?


01:15:32.911 --> 01:15:36.438
If I say this asshole can leave,
would anybody contradict me?


01:15:36.514 --> 01:15:38.141
No one, Captain.
He can leave.


01:15:38.884 --> 01:15:43.014
There you have it.
Count to three.


01:15:59.404 --> 01:16:02.032
- One.
- Good.


01:16:06.278 --> 01:16:07.245
Two.


01:16:09.014 --> 01:16:11.915
One more and you will be free.


01:16:28.833 --> 01:16:29.800
Shame.


01:16:41.713 --> 01:16:45.740
Your mother is much better,
Your Highness.


01:16:47.185 --> 01:16:53.249
Surely, you must be relieved.


01:16:53.758 --> 01:16:55.851
Yes, thank you.


01:16:56.261 --> 01:16:59.719
But things haven't turned out so well.


01:17:00.632 --> 01:17:01.724
No?


01:17:03.535 --> 01:17:07.164
- I had an accident.
- An accident?


01:17:07.339 --> 01:17:08.306
Yes.


01:17:17.582 --> 01:17:20.483
- You broke the rules!
- It was only two grapes!


01:17:20.585 --> 01:17:22.177
I thought no one would notice.


01:17:23.588 --> 01:17:26.682
- We've made a mistake!
- A mistake?


01:17:27.425 --> 01:17:31.156
You failed.
You can never return.


01:17:31.262 --> 01:17:34.925
- It was an accident!
- You cannot return.


01:17:35.033 --> 01:17:38.992
The moon will be full in three days.


01:17:39.571 --> 01:17:45.271
Your spirit shall forever remain
among the humans.


01:17:45.377 --> 01:17:49.245
You shall age like them,
you shall die like them


01:17:49.314 --> 01:17:53.410
and all memory of you
shall fade in time.


01:17:53.985 --> 01:17:57.978
And we'll vanish along with it.


01:17:58.623 --> 01:18:02.423
You will never see us again.


01:18:13.138 --> 01:18:16.869
Good day, doctor.
Sorry to wake you so early,


01:18:17.609 --> 01:18:19.338
but I think we need your help.


01:18:42.667 --> 01:18:44.225
My God, what have you done to him?


01:18:44.402 --> 01:18:45.528
Not much.


01:18:47.472 --> 01:18:49.269
But things are getting better.


01:18:57.182 --> 01:19:01.915
I like having you handy, Doctor.
It has its advantages.


01:19:03.455 --> 01:19:04.922
Serrano, stay here.


01:19:05.090 --> 01:19:06.148
I talked.


01:19:07.559 --> 01:19:08.787
Not much.


01:19:11.162 --> 01:19:14.598
- B-b-but I talked.
- I'm sorry.


01:19:15.333 --> 01:19:16.925
I'm so sorry.


01:19:24.075 --> 01:19:29.206
Kill me.
Kill me now, please.


01:19:45.396 --> 01:19:46.988
Son of a bitch.


01:20:08.086 --> 01:20:10.020
It'll take away the pain.


01:20:16.394 --> 01:20:17.861
It's almost over.


01:20:26.604 --> 01:20:27.935
Watch Dr. Ferreiro,


01:20:28.072 --> 01:20:29.539
- I'll be right there.
- Yes, Captain.


01:20:53.097 --> 01:20:54.689
You're not moving anymore.


01:20:56.201 --> 01:20:57.634
Are you sick?


01:21:00.838 --> 01:21:03.363
What are you doing down there?


01:21:16.955 --> 01:21:18.616
- Call him!
- Who?


01:21:18.723 --> 01:21:21.123
Who else, you imbecile?
Ferreiro!


01:21:45.216 --> 01:21:47.309
What the hell is this?


01:21:50.388 --> 01:21:51.980
No! No, no!


01:21:52.223 --> 01:21:55.818
Leave her.
Leave her alone, please!


01:21:57.528 --> 01:22:00.088
Look at this! Look what she
was hiding under your bed!


01:22:00.498 --> 01:22:01.692
What do you think of this?


01:22:06.304 --> 01:22:10.798
Ofelia, what is this thing doing
under the bed?


01:22:11.009 --> 01:22:14.945
It's a magic root
the faun gave me.


01:22:15.113 --> 01:22:17.707
This is all because of thatjunk
you let her read.


01:22:18.049 --> 01:22:19.016
Look what you've done!


01:22:19.150 --> 01:22:23.211
Please, leave us alone.
I'll talk to her, darling.


01:22:23.855 --> 01:22:26.790
Fine.
As you wish.


01:22:28.593 --> 01:22:31.289
He told me you would get better.
And you did.


01:22:31.562 --> 01:22:34.463
Ofelia, you have to listen
to your father.


01:22:35.800 --> 01:22:36.892
You have to stop all this.


01:22:37.568 --> 01:22:40.196
No. I want to leave this place!


01:22:40.538 --> 01:22:43.701
Please, take me away from here!
Let's just go, Please!


01:22:43.841 --> 01:22:46.139
Things are not that simple.


01:22:48.379 --> 01:22:50.210
You're getting older,


01:22:51.249 --> 01:22:54.616
soon you'll see that life
isn't like your fairy tales.


01:22:55.219 --> 01:22:57.414
The world is a cruel place.


01:22:58.790 --> 01:23:02.521
And you'll learn that,
even if it hurts.


01:23:04.128 --> 01:23:06.653
- No! No!
- Ofelia!


01:23:07.999 --> 01:23:12.959
Magic does not exist.
Not for you, me or anyone else.


01:23:24.782 --> 01:23:27.046
Mom! Help!


01:23:27.518 --> 01:23:28.951
Help!


01:23:29.821 --> 01:23:31.083
Help!


01:23:37.128 --> 01:23:38.095
Why did you do it?


01:23:40.431 --> 01:23:42.092
It was the only thing I could do.


01:23:43.434 --> 01:23:45.664
No. You could have obeyed me.


01:23:47.438 --> 01:23:49.702
I could have, but I didn't.


01:23:51.642 --> 01:23:54.167
It would have been better for you.
You know it.


01:23:55.580 --> 01:23:58.549
I don't understand.
Why didn't you obey me?


01:23:58.850 --> 01:24:04.982
To obey-just like that-for the sake
of obeying, without questioning...


01:24:06.724 --> 01:24:09.716
that's something only people
like you can do, Captain.


01:24:47.165 --> 01:24:48.496
Captain!


01:24:54.806 --> 01:24:57.172
Garces! Call the troop paramedic.


01:24:57.375 --> 01:24:59.866
- Get up immediately!
- Yes, Captain.


01:25:34.512 --> 01:25:36.377
Your wife is dead.


01:25:46.057 --> 01:25:49.549
Because the paths to the Lord
are inscrutable.


01:25:50.027 --> 01:25:51.892
Because the essence
of His forgiveness


01:25:51.963 --> 01:25:55.296
lies in His word
and in His mystery.


01:25:56.167 --> 01:25:59.159
Because although God
sends us the message,


01:25:59.303 --> 01:26:01.931
it is our task to decipher it.


01:26:02.807 --> 01:26:04.638
Because when we open our arms


01:26:04.809 --> 01:26:09.678
the earth takes in only a hollow
and senseless shell.


01:26:11.048 --> 01:26:13.983
Far away now is the soul
in its eternal glory.


01:26:14.585 --> 01:26:18.248
Because it is in pain
that we find the meaning of life.


01:26:19.056 --> 01:26:21.991
And the state of grace
that we lose when we are born.


01:26:23.327 --> 01:26:28.594
Because God, in His infinite wisdom,
puts the solution in our hands.


01:26:32.670 --> 01:26:35.161
And because it is only
in His physical absence,


01:26:35.339 --> 01:26:39.605
that the place He occupies
in our souls is reaffirmed.


01:27:01.566 --> 01:27:05.058
You knew
Dr. Ferreiro pretty well,
didn't you, Mercedes?


01:27:06.137 --> 01:27:09.072
We all knew him, sir.
Everyone around here.


01:27:11.042 --> 01:27:14.671
The stutterer spoke of an informer.
Here... at the mill.


01:27:15.846 --> 01:27:19.714
Can you imagine?
Right under my nose.


01:27:21.552 --> 01:27:24.988
Mercedes, please.


01:27:34.732 --> 01:27:36.165
What must you think of me?


01:27:37.435 --> 01:27:39.027
You must think that
I'm a monster.


01:27:39.570 --> 01:27:42.471
It doesn't matter
what someone like me thinks, sir.


01:27:52.650 --> 01:27:55.551
I want you to the storehouse
and bring me some more liquor, please.


01:27:55.820 --> 01:27:59.017
Yes, sir.
Goodnight, sir.


01:27:59.590 --> 01:28:03.549
Mercedes,
aren't you forgetting something?


01:28:04.595 --> 01:28:05.584
Sir?


01:28:10.635 --> 01:28:11.533
The key.


01:28:12.570 --> 01:28:14.902
I do have the only copy, don't I?


01:28:16.107 --> 01:28:17.096
Yes, sir.


01:28:18.643 --> 01:28:22.636
You know, there's an odd detail
that's been bothering me.


01:28:22.980 --> 01:28:24.914
Maybe it's not important, but...


01:28:25.182 --> 01:28:26.774
the day they broke into
the storehouse,


01:28:27.018 --> 01:28:29.350
with all those grenades
and explosives,


01:28:30.254 --> 01:28:31.744
the lock itself wasn't forced.


01:28:34.058 --> 01:28:37.653
As I said, it's probably
not important.


01:28:41.265 --> 01:28:42.562
Be very careful.


01:28:44.669 --> 01:28:45.897
Good night, sir.


01:29:28.746 --> 01:29:31.510
Ofelia, Ofelia!


01:29:31.782 --> 01:29:33.807
Ofelia, I'm leaving tonight.


01:29:34.351 --> 01:29:37.843
- Where to?
- I can't tell you. I can't tell you...


01:29:37.955 --> 01:29:40.981
- Take me with you.
- No, no. I can't.


01:29:41.092 --> 01:29:44.118
I can't, my child. But I'll come
back for you, I promise.


01:29:44.261 --> 01:29:45.387
Take me with you.


01:30:10.287 --> 01:30:11.584
I heard something.


01:30:16.560 --> 01:30:19.723
It's nothing, don't worry.


01:30:29.073 --> 01:30:30.062
Mercedes.


01:30:32.243 --> 01:30:33.210
Ofelia.


01:30:42.219 --> 01:30:43.846
How long have
you known about her?


01:30:49.260 --> 01:30:50.818
How long have you been
laughing at me?


01:30:51.061 --> 01:30:52.255
Little bitch!


01:30:53.597 --> 01:30:54.859
Watch her!


01:30:58.335 --> 01:31:00.064
And if anyone tries to get in,


01:31:01.038 --> 01:31:02.630
kill her first.


01:31:16.954 --> 01:31:17.921
Dry meat.


01:31:21.525 --> 01:31:22.514
Tobacco.


01:31:23.828 --> 01:31:26.592
If you had asked for it, I would have
given this to you, Mercedes.


01:31:33.804 --> 01:31:36.034
I want the names of whoever
wrote these letters.


01:31:37.775 --> 01:31:39.936
And I want them
in front of me, tomorrow.


01:31:40.311 --> 01:31:41.335
Yes, Captain.


01:31:44.215 --> 01:31:45.682
You can go, Garces.


01:31:47.251 --> 01:31:48.650
You're sure, Captain?


01:31:51.088 --> 01:31:53.852
For God's sake,
she's just a woman.


01:31:57.828 --> 01:31:59.989
That's what you've always thought.


01:32:01.165 --> 01:32:03.963
That's why I was able to get away with it.


01:32:04.201 --> 01:32:08.865
- I was invisible to you.
- Damn.


01:32:09.707 --> 01:32:13.507
You've found my weakness:
Pride.


01:32:14.912 --> 01:32:18.245
But it's your weak points
we're interested in.


01:32:20.618 --> 01:32:23.553
It's very simple: You will talk...


01:32:25.256 --> 01:32:26.280
And I have to know


01:32:28.259 --> 01:32:29.556
that everything you say is the truth.


01:32:30.794 --> 01:32:35.060
We have a few things here
strictly for that purpose.


01:32:37.001 --> 01:32:38.263
Nothing complicated.


01:32:41.105 --> 01:32:42.629
Things we learn on the job.


01:32:44.742 --> 01:32:46.710
At first...


01:33:03.827 --> 01:33:07.058
I'm not some old man!
Not a wounded prisoner!


01:33:07.131 --> 01:33:11.192
Mother Fucker!
Don't you dare touch the girl?


01:33:11.435 --> 01:33:13.198
Won't be the first pig I gutted.


01:33:36.694 --> 01:33:37.786
Look! He let her go.


01:33:40.297 --> 01:33:41.594
The fuck did you say?


01:33:49.606 --> 01:33:52.302
Get her!
Come on! Bring her to me!


01:33:52.743 --> 01:33:54.574
Bring her to me, damn it!


01:33:54.712 --> 01:33:56.202
Mount up!


01:34:59.143 --> 01:35:01.634
Lt'll be better if you come
with me without struggling.


01:35:02.279 --> 01:35:04.304
The Captain said that if you behave...


01:35:08.952 --> 01:35:10.715
Don't be a fool, sweetheart.


01:35:11.088 --> 01:35:12.646
If anyone's going to kill you...


01:35:14.758 --> 01:35:15.952
I'd rather it be me.


01:36:26.330 --> 01:36:31.267
I've decided to give you
one last chance.


01:36:36.540 --> 01:36:38.235
Do you promise to do what I say?


01:36:40.244 --> 01:36:44.476
Will you do everything I tell you,
without question?


01:36:46.283 --> 01:36:49.252
This is your last chance.


01:36:50.387 --> 01:36:53.515
Then listen to me.


01:36:53.957 --> 01:36:56.357
Fetch your brother


01:36:56.760 --> 01:36:59.422
and bring him to the labyrinth,


01:36:59.563 --> 01:37:03.966
as quickly as you can,
Your Highness.


01:37:04.201 --> 01:37:05.532
My brother?


01:37:05.769 --> 01:37:07.100
We need him.


01:37:07.237 --> 01:37:10.297
- But...
- No more questions.


01:37:13.310 --> 01:37:14.868
The door's locked.


01:37:15.879 --> 01:37:21.784
In that case,
create your own door.


01:40:10.420 --> 01:40:11.853
Captain, with your permission.


01:40:15.225 --> 01:40:16.249
Come quickly.


01:40:17.027 --> 01:40:20.292
- Now what?
- Serrano is back. He's wounded.


01:40:21.264 --> 01:40:22.629
Wounded?


01:41:08.845 --> 01:41:10.244
Where's Garces?


01:41:17.721 --> 01:41:18.710
How many were there?


01:41:19.256 --> 01:41:21.486
I don't know exactly, Captain.


01:41:21.925 --> 01:41:23.415
Fifty men, at least.


01:41:23.527 --> 01:41:27.122
The rest of the men didn't make it.
Our watch posts are not responding.


01:41:27.264 --> 01:41:30.859
- How many men we have left?
- Twenty, maybe less, sir.


01:41:41.678 --> 01:41:45.045
We're leaving.
Together.


01:41:46.082 --> 01:41:47.344
Don't be afraid.


01:41:48.218 --> 01:41:49.879
Nothing is going to happen to you.


01:41:56.259 --> 01:41:57.886
Put them on picket duty
at the tree line.


01:41:58.028 --> 01:42:00.155
If the rest of the squad gets back,
have it report immediately to me.


01:42:00.397 --> 01:42:03.889
Radio for reinforcements, now.


01:42:04.067 --> 01:42:05.364
Yes, Captain.


01:42:32.195 --> 01:42:33.423
Leave him!


01:43:19.509 --> 01:43:20.771
Ofelia!


01:44:47.931 --> 01:44:50.627
Quickly, Your Majesty,


01:44:50.900 --> 01:44:53.425
give him to me.


01:44:53.970 --> 01:44:57.064
The full moon is high in the sky,


01:44:57.173 --> 01:45:00.006
we can open the portal.


01:45:00.910 --> 01:45:02.537
Why is that in your hand?


01:45:04.047 --> 01:45:08.950
The portal will only open
if we offer the blood of an innocent.


01:45:09.252 --> 01:45:13.689
Just a drop of blood.
A pinprick, that's all.


01:45:13.790 --> 01:45:16.384
It's the final task.


01:45:16.693 --> 01:45:18.024
Hurry.


01:45:20.730 --> 01:45:23.824
You promised to obey me!


01:45:24.267 --> 01:45:26.497
- Give me the boy!
- No!


01:45:27.103 --> 01:45:29.230
My brother stays with me.


01:45:29.472 --> 01:45:35.377
You would give up your sacred rights
for this brat you barely know?


01:45:35.445 --> 01:45:38.243
Yes, I would.


01:45:39.549 --> 01:45:42.017
You would give up
your throne for him?


01:45:42.152 --> 01:45:46.748
He who has caused you
such misery, such humiliation?


01:45:47.290 --> 01:45:50.157
Yes, I would.


01:45:54.264 --> 01:45:59.964
As you wish, Your Highness.


01:46:15.685 --> 01:46:16.709
No!


01:47:15.411 --> 01:47:16.400
My son.


01:47:44.007 --> 01:47:45.668
Tell my son...


01:47:51.514 --> 01:47:53.607
Tell him what time his father died.


01:47:54.417 --> 01:47:55.714
- Tell him that I...
- No.


01:47:56.920 --> 01:47:58.683
He won't even know your name.


01:49:41.524 --> 01:49:43.549
Arise, my daughter.


01:49:46.863 --> 01:49:48.125
Come.


01:50:14.357 --> 01:50:15.585
Father.


01:50:16.092 --> 01:50:19.721
You have spilled your own blood
rather than that of an innocent.


01:50:20.496 --> 01:50:24.330
That was the final task,
and the most important.


01:50:34.844 --> 01:50:40.111
And you chose well,
Your Highness.


01:50:40.350 --> 01:50:42.011
Come here with me,


01:50:42.885 --> 01:50:45.012
and sit by your father's side.


01:50:45.488 --> 01:50:47.683
He's been waiting for you so long.


01:51:40.610 --> 01:51:44.376
And it is said the princess
returned to her father's kingdom.


01:51:45.314 --> 01:51:50.650
That she reigned there with justice
and a kind heart for many centuries.


01:51:51.554 --> 01:51:53.818
That she was loved by her people.


01:51:54.090 --> 01:51:58.789
And that she left behind
small traces of her time on earth,


01:51:59.896 --> 01:52:04.731
visible only to those
who know where to look.

